# once_nothing: S4, the source of C1 and A1, says "there could have been nothing", a mere possibility. S5–S6, the source of P5, reason from "if at one time nothing was in existence", an actual past state. The first sense is true only if such a time really occurred; the second only needs it to be possible.
# The step in A1 from "each contingent thing at some time is not" to "at one time all are not" is a scope shift rather than a change in a word's sense, so it is not marked.
# necessary_exists: "necessary" in S7 means "not possible not to be". S8–S10 allow necessity caused by another. I took these as the same sense, but I was less sure here.
